Package: rquasar
Title: Survey Microdata to Publication Tables with a 'Rust' Backend
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Juan Marcelo", "Gutierrez Miranda", , "info@todoeconometria.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4452-7934"))
Description: Reads survey microdata in the formats used by statistical
    offices ('SPSS', 'Stata', 'SAS', fixed-width files with record layouts,
    'Excel', 'dBase', 'Parquet'), recodes survey missing values, builds
    codebooks and produces weighted tabulations with design-based standard
    errors (via 'survey', Lumley (2004) <doi:10.18637/jss.v009.i08>),
    regression tables and plots from a single registered context. Poverty
    measures of the Foster, Greer and Thorbecke (1984)
    <doi:10.2307/1913475> family and inequality indices (Gini, Theil,
    Atkinson) are estimated with linearization or replicate-weight standard
    errors (Langel and Tille (2013) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-985X.2012.01048.x>),
    by domain. Large delimited files are filtered, grouped and converted to
    'Parquet' in bounded memory by a 'Rust' backend built on 'Polars'.
